---
/** A registry in full: the ready-made rules next to a repo's own, as one exported array. */
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import source from '../../../snippets/lint-meta/registry.mts?raw';
---

<section class="nc-section nc-sample not-content" aria-labelledby="nc-sample-title">
  <div class="nc-sample__text">
    <h2 id="nc-sample-title">Your rules, in your repo.</h2>
    <p>
      <code>harness lint-meta</code> imports one file, the registry, and runs the rules it exports. The
      generic ones come from <code>@noctcore/harness/rules</code>; yours sit beside them.
    </p>
    <ol class="nc-steps">
      <li><span>The registry exports <code>META_RULES</code>, an array of rule objects.</span></li>
      <li><span>Each rule reads the repo through <code>ctx</code> and returns its violations.</span></li>
      <li><span>A violation from a CI-critical rule, or a rule that throws, exits 1.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="nc-sample__code">
    <Code code={source.trimEnd()} lang="ts" title=".nightcore/lint-meta/registry.mts" />
  </div>
</section>
